---
import Since from '../../components/Since.astro';
import Snippet from '../../components/Snippet.astro';
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';

const html = `<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8" />
<title>zvuk · music</title>
<button id="start">Start</button>
<button id="win" disabled>Win: outro on the bar</button>
<button id="stop" disabled>Stop now</button>
<button id="pause" disabled>Pause</button>
<button id="sting" disabled>Stinger on next bar</button>
<p id="part">idle</p>
<script type="module" src="./main.ts"></script>`;

const main = `import { createEngine, type MusicVoice } from '@schmooky/zvuk';

const engine = createEngine({ buses: { music: { level: 0.8 }, sfx: {} } });
const $ = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLButtonElement;

let voice: MusicVoice | null = null;

$('start').onclick = async () => {
  await engine.unlock();
  const music = engine.hasMusic('bonus')
    ? engine.music('bonus')
    : await engine.loadMusic(
        'bonus',
        {
          intro: ['/music/bonus-intro.webm', '/music/bonus-intro.m4a'],
          loop: ['/music/bonus-loop.webm', '/music/bonus-loop.m4a'],
          outro: ['/music/bonus-outro.webm', '/music/bonus-outro.m4a'],
        },
        { bus: 'music', loopCrossfade: 0.02, bpm: 128, beatsPerBar: 4 },
      );
  if (!engine.hasSound('sting')) {
    await engine.loadSound('sting', ['/sfx/sting.webm', '/sfx/sting.m4a'], { bus: 'sfx' });
  }

  voice?.stop({ fade: 0.2 });
  voice = music.play({ fadeIn: 0.05 });
  for (const id of ['win', 'stop', 'pause', 'sting']) $(id).disabled = false;

  // currentPart walks intro → loop → outro → ended on the audio clock.
  const tick = () => {
    $('part').textContent = voice?.currentPart ?? 'idle';
    if (voice && voice.currentPart !== 'ended') requestAnimationFrame(tick);
  };
  tick();

  await voice.ended;
  for (const id of ['win', 'stop', 'pause', 'sting']) $(id).disabled = true;
};

// v2: end on the next bar of the 128 bpm grid, not at the end of the loop file.
$('win').onclick = () => voice?.skipToOutro({ at: 'bar' });

// v2: pause keeps the part and offset; resume lands in the same place.
$('pause').onclick = () => {
  if (!voice) return;
  if (voice.isPaused) voice.resume();
  else voice.pause();
  $('pause').textContent = voice.isPaused ? 'Resume' : 'Pause';
};

// v2: a stinger on the next downbeat, ducking the music while it rings.
$('sting').onclick = () => {
  const at = voice?.nextBar();
  if (at !== undefined) engine.sound('sting').play({ at, duck: { bus: 'music', amount: 0.5 } });
};

// Cut to the outro immediately, with a short equal-power fade.
$('stop').onclick = () => voice?.skipToOutro({ at: 'now' });`;
---
<Docs
  title="Music: intro, loop, outro"
  description="A three-part track where the stinger plays once, the loop runs until told otherwise, and the outro lands on a loop boundary. Two files to copy."
  eyebrow="Example"
>
  <p>
    The bonus round starts with a stinger, sits in a loop for as long as the
    player keeps winning, and has to end on the beat when they stop. Starting
    the outro wherever the playhead happens to be sounds like a mistake.
  </p>
  <p>
    <code>engine.loadMusic</code> <Since v="1.8" /> fetches the three parts in
    parallel and returns a <code>Music</code>. Each <code>play()</code>
    returns a <code>MusicVoice</code> whose <code>skipToOutro()</code>
    either waits for the next loop boundary or cuts over now. Drop your own
    files at the paths below; any part except <code>loop</code> is optional.
  </p>
  <p>
    With <code>bpm</code> on the load <Since v="2.0" />, the voice knows
    where the bars are: <code>skipToOutro({'{'} at: 'bar' {'}'})</code> ends on
    the grid, and <code>nextBar()</code> gives an audio time for
    <code>play({'{'} at {'}'})</code>. <code>pause()</code> and <code>resume()</code>
    <Since v="2.0" /> keep the part and offset. The
    <a href="/concepts/music/">Music</a> page has the same thing running live.
  </p>

  <h2>index.html</h2>
  <Snippet code={html} lang="html" title="index.html" />

  <h2>main.ts</h2>
  <Snippet code={main} lang="ts" title="main.ts" />

  <h2>Notes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <code>loopCrossfade</code> hides a click at the loop seam when the file
      wasn't cut on a zero crossing. 20 ms is enough for most material; leave
      it at 0 for a sample-exact loop.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>voice.stop()</code> skips the outro entirely. Call
      <code>skipToOutro()</code> when you want the tail.
    </li>
    <li>
      <code>music.voices()</code> and <code>music.stopAll()</code> reach every
      voice a <code>Music</code> has spawned, which helps when a scene change
      has lost track of them.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Related</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/concepts/music/">Music</a> concept page.</li>
    <li><a href="/examples/stream/">StreamSound</a> for tracks too long to decode.</li>
    <li><a href="/examples/">All examples</a></li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
